      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory RTO Paperwork, Transit Marine Insurance &amp; Delivery Handover for Bikes Cars Domestic Vehicle</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When arranging domestic transport for a motor vehicle, the paperwork required for a bike differs in detail from that of a car, yet both share a core set of documents that must be completed, verified, and presented to the carrier.</p>
<p>Below is a concise guide to the essential paperwork for each type of vehicle, with an emphasis on the 100 % declared‑value marine transit insurance that protects the asset throughout the journey.</p>

<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(230px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px;">
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #f59e0b22; color: #f59e0b; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">01</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Self‑attested RC Photocopy</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">A clear photocopy of the Registration Certificate (RC) is mandatory for both bikes and cars. For bikes, the photocopy should include the vehicle’s engine number and chassis number, while for cars it must show the Vehicle Identification Number (VIN).</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin-top: 14px; margin-bottom: 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); padding-top: 10px;">
  <li style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 0.84rem; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 6px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 8px;">
    <i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; font-size: 0.8rem; margin-top: 3px; flex-shrink: 0;"></i>
    <span>The document must be self‑attested by the owner or an authorized representative</span>
  </li>
</ul>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #10b98122; color: #10b981; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">02</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Current Pollution Under Control (PUC) Certificate</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">A valid PUC is required for all vehicles. Bikes generally have a shorter validity period (one year) compared to cars (one year for new and three years for old), so verify the expiration date before booking the transport.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Valid Insurance Certificate</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The carrier will request proof of insurance that covers the vehicle’s value during transit. For bikes, a third‑party liability policy is often sufficient, but for cars, a comprehensive policy that includes collision, theft, and natural disasters is advisable.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #a855f722; color: #a855f7; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">04</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">IBA‑Approved Consignment Bilty</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">This consignment document, issued by the International Bilty Association (IBA), is compulsory for all domestic vehicle shipments. It acts as a receipt, confirming the vehicle’s handover and detailing the agreed freight charges, pickup and delivery dates, and any special handling instructions.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<p>Beyond these documents, the carrier will typically request the following supporting paperwork:</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>Vehicle Inspection Report</strong> – A pre‑transport inspection form that lists any existing damage and the vehicle’s condition.</li>
<li><strong>Roadworthiness Certificate</strong> – Especially important for cars that have not been driven for an extended period.</li>
<li><strong>Export/Import Clearance (if applicable)</strong> – For cross‑border shipments or for vehicles that have recently been imported.</li>
</ul>

<p>All of the above documents must be compiled into a single package and submitted to the transport provider at least 48 hours before the scheduled pickup. Failure to provide complete documentation can result in delays, fines, or even the refusal of transport services.</p>

<p><strong>100 % Declared‑Value Marine Transit Insurance</strong> is a specialized policy that covers the full value of the vehicle in case of loss or damage during marine transit. For high‑value cars or premium bikes, this insurance ensures that the owner receives a full reimbursement without the need to prove a lower market value.</p>
<p>It is highly recommended for any vehicle with a valuation above ₹10 lakh, as it protects against unforeseen events such as shipwreck, cargo mishandling, or theft during the transit period.</p>

<p>By preparing the above paperwork meticulously and opting for 100 % declared‑value marine transit insurance, vehicle owners can ensure a smooth, secure, and hassle‑free transport experience.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


